3. Toggling a bit at nth positionToggling means to turn bit 'on'(1) if it was 'off'(0) and to turn 'off'(0) if it was 'on'(1) previously. We will be using the 'XOR' operator here which is this '^'. The reason behind the 'XOR' operator is because of its properties.Properties of 'XOR' operator. 1^1 = 00^0 = 01^0 = 10^1 = 1If two bits are different then the 'XOR' operator returns a set bit(1) else it returns an unset bit(0).
